# Round 105's control: with every builtin-name arm now gated on the
# name not being a user function, the UNSHADOWED forms must still take
# their fast paths -- the SIMD reductions, the C intrinsics, and the
# buffer-length read. This is the other side of t194's branch, kept in
# its own program because t194 shadows the names globally.
a is buffer of 4
b is buffer of 4
for i in range of 4:
    a[i] is i + 1
    b[i] is i + 2
print of (dot of [a, b])
print of (sum of a)
print of (norm of a)
print of (sqrt of 16)
print of (exp of 0)
print of (len of a)
